          ],
          "current": "Charts as code: dashboards that ship with their models"
        },
        "tag": "Upcoming",
        "title": "Charts as code: dashboards that ship with their models",
        "blocks": [
          {
            "kind": "p",
            "text": "Dashboards are where carefully defined metrics most often drift. A definition is reviewed in the project and then rebuilt a little differently in a reporting tool."
          },
          {
            "kind": "p",
            "text": "In this live session the team behind Lattice Charts shows how to keep simple dashboards in the same repository as the models that feed them."
          },
          {
            "kind": "p",
            "text": "You will watch a chart get defined in a short file, approved alongside a change to its metric and built during that very run. When a test fails, the chart keeps showing the last good version with a clear note for readers, so nobody makes a decision from a half-updated view. We will also cover sharing, permissions and how charts fit alongside the reporting tools your company already uses, including when a full business intelligence tool is still the better choice."
          },
          {
            "kind": "p",
            "text": "The second half of the session is a hands-on walkthrough. Bring a project if you have one; if not, we will share a sample repository you can follow along with in a free workspace."
          },
          {
            "kind": "p",
            "text": "All registrants receive the recording, the sample repository and a summary of the questions answered during the session."
          },
          {
            "kind": "p",
            "text": "Seats are limited for the live session."
          },
          {
            "kind": "ul",
            "items": [
              {
                "text": "Define a chart in a few lines of configuration and preview it in the editor before opening a pull request."
              },
              {
                "text": "Review a metric change and the chart that shows it together, with a rendered preview attached to the request."
              },
              {
                "text": "See how failed tests protect readers by keeping the last good version of a chart on display with a note."
              },
              {
                "text": "Learn when to use charts as code and when a dedicated reporting tool is the better fit for your team."
              }
            ]
          },
          {
            "kind": "accordion",
            "items": [
              {
                "q": "Who should attend?",
                "blocks": [
                  {
                    "kind": "ul",
                    "items": [
                      {
                        "text": "Analytics engineers"
                      },
                      {
                        "text": "Analysts who own dashboards"
                      },
                      {
                        "text": "Data team leads"
                      }
                    ]
                  }
                ]
              },
              {
                "q": "What to prepare",
                "blocks": [
                  {
                    "kind": "ul",
                    "items": [
                      {
                        "text": "A free workspace"
                      },
                      {
                        "text": "A metric you check weekly"
                      },
                      {
                        "text": "Your questions"
                      }
                    ]
                  }
                ]
              }
            ]
          },
          {
            "kind": "hosts",
            "title": "Meet your hosts",
            "people": [
              {
                "name": "Noor Haddad",
                "role": "Product",
                "avatar": {
                  "assetRole": "person.fictional-avatar",
                  "alt": "",
                  "ref": "/assets/pages/people/avatar-5.svg"
                }
              },
              {
